{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RothInductionHypothesis","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RothInductionHypothesis","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SeparatedGauss","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RothLemmaStatement","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.WronskianHeight"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.index_rescaled_wronskian_le_theta_witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.index_rescaled_wronskian_le_theta_witness","kind":"theorem","line":350,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothInductionHypothesis.lean#L350-L394","doc":"**Non-vacuity of the `Θ` form.**\n\nSame data as `index_rescaled_wronskian_le_witness` — one variable each side, everything\nconstant — with `IsRothTheta` supplied by `exists_isRothTheta` and the point `κ = 1`, whose\nheight `max(1,1)` is exactly the required `H = 1`.\n\n⚠ The hypothesis stack is **shorter** than the `RothLemmaUniform` version's: no `Kh`, no `E`,\nno coprimality, no `2 ≤ Kh`, no `RothGamma`, and no `r ≠ 0`.  That is the practical evidence for\ncorrection nineteen — the faithful form of §12's step asks for less because it asks for the\nright thing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.index_rescaled_wronskian_le_right_theta_div","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.index_rescaled_wronskian_le_right_theta_div","kind":"theorem","line":320,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothInductionHypothesis.lean#L320-L348","doc":"**The `y` half of `hres`, in `Θ` form, against the divided Wronskian** — correction 26. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.index_rescaled_wronskian_le_theta_div","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.index_rescaled_wronskian_le_theta_div","kind":"theorem","line":290,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothInductionHypothesis.lean#L290-L318","doc":"**The `x` half of `hres`, in `Θ` form, against the divided Wronskian** — correction 26. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.index_rescaled_wronskian_le_right_theta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.index_rescaled_wronskian_le_right_theta","kind":"theorem","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothInductionHypothesis.lean#L242-L271","doc":"**The `y` half of `hres`, in `Θ` form** — §12's `J(V; ρ_m; κ_m) ≤ Θ₁(b; ρ_m; H_m)`.\n\nThe mirror, and it needs no induction hypothesis: the split-off group is one variable, so the\n`Θ` it is measured against is `Θ₁`, which §10 bounds outright (`isRothTheta_le_of_gamma_one`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.index_rescaled_wronskian_le_theta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.index_rescaled_wronskian_le_theta","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothInductionHypothesis.lean#L210-L240","doc":"**The `x` half of `hres`, in `Θ` form** — §12's `J(U;ρ;κ) ≤ Θ_{m−1}(b;ρ;H)`.\n\n§6's Gauss replaces the rational Wronskian by an integral `U'` with `map U' = C l · W_x`; `U'`\nthen lies in `R(b; r·d₁)` by the degree and height bounds; `IsRothTheta`'s first clause applies;\nand `index_C_mul` carries the bound back, the scaling being free on the index side. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.index_rescaled_wronskian_le_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.index_rescaled_wronskian_le_right","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothInductionHypothesis.lean#L141-L190","doc":"**The `y` half of `hres`** — and it needs **no induction hypothesis at all**.\n\nThe split-off group is a single variable, so the relevant instance of `RothLemmaUniform` is\nthe `m = 1` case, which is `rothLemmaUniform_one` and is **proved**.  So where the `x` half\nconsumes the induction hypothesis, this half consumes the base case, and the recursion's two\ninputs turn out to be the same theorem at two different arities.\n\nThe growth condition does not appear: at one variable there is no consecutive pair, so\n`RothGrowth` is vacuous — which is also why `rothLemmaUniform_one` holds for every `ω`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.index_rescaled_wronskian_le_witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.index_rescaled_wronskian_le_witness","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothInductionHypothesis.lean#L83-L139","doc":"**Non-vacuity.**  The largest hypothesis stack in this arc, shown jointly satisfiable.\n\nOne variable on each side, everything constant: `n = r = 1`, `d₁ ≡ 1`, `P = 1`, `φ = ψ ≡ 1`,\n`p/q = 1/2`, `B = 1`, `E = 0`.  Then the auxiliary polynomial's determinant is `1`, whose\ncoefficients are `0` and `1`, so `B = 1` works; `E = 0` makes `B ≤ q^E` read `1 ≤ 1`; and the\ninduction hypothesis is `rothLemmaUniform_one`, which is **proved**.\n\n⚠ This certifies joint satisfiability and nothing more — and the arc has been explicit that\nfinite witnesses test vacuity, not usefulness (correction 9). What it rules out is the failure\nmode that a stack this large invites: two side conditions that quietly contradict each other,\nleaving a theorem that is true because it is empty. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.index_rescaled_wronskian_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.index_rescaled_wronskian_le","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothInductionHypothesis.lean#L37-L81","doc":"**The `x` half of `hres`, from the induction hypothesis.**\n\nRead the hypotheses as the induction step supplies them: `φ`, `ψ` are a separated\nrepresentation of the (integer) auxiliary polynomial `P`, `Dx`, `Dy` a bounded-order operator\nfamily with both Wronskians non-zero, and `B` a height bound on the determinant those\noperators form over `ℤ`.\n\n⚠ `hWy` — the `y`-Wronskian being non-zero — is needed for the **height** step and nothing\nelse: `abs_coeff_le_of_mul_separated` picks a non-zero coefficient of the other factor. It is\nexactly what `BoundedOrderWronskian` supplies, and it is the same hypothesis §7 leans on. ","signatureChunk":0}]}